  {
    "episode_id": 43480,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/3/43480.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 72,
    "turn_text": "Well, if I can editorialize for a second, as a longtime staffer in Congress, it used to drive me crazy. It still does. When I hear people sort of at writ large, say members of Congress, politicians, they compare them to the most vile order of human being out there, which, first of all, on this day and age is extremely dangerous. But second of all is so at odds with my experience. And I hope that people who've been watching this on video and listening on pod or on radio have gotten a flavor for this in listening to setter or hike camp because it really is amazing. Your command of the issues and the politics and what it means to represent people where you come from. And also think about the interests of America and the way your story embodies the best of what this country is about. I have to say that that was basically the norm",
